  "notes": [
    "Every product, category, tag, attribute, image, customer, order, review, tax rate, shipping zone and setting is synthetic, created by the commands below on an empty WooCommerce. No WooCommerce sample data was imported.",
    "Answers are WooCommerce's JSON bodies parsed and written back with 2-space indent; no value is changed. List requests are exactly the ones the importer sends (per_page=100, orderby=id, order=asc); every page is recorded with its X-WP-Total and X-WP-TotalPages.",
    "A list that fits one page is <name>.json (categories, customers, orders, reviews, coupons, taxes); products, which take two pages, are products.page-<n>.json.",
    "coupons, taxes and shipping zones are the plan's own probes (count only, per_page=1 for coupons and taxes, /shipping/zones unpaginated); coupons and taxes are recorded at per_page=100 so a server can answer either size. An empty coupons list answers X-WP-TotalPages 0.",
    "HPOS is on: wp wc hpos enable made the orders tables before any order existed, so orders are authoritative in them with sync off. An order id and a post id share one sequence, so order ids skip 153, the refund.",
    "Orders were created through REST with set_paid (status processing, stock reduced) and then set to completed, so recorded product stock is after the orders. WooCommerce computed every tax and total; each order total equals its lines, shipping and fees with their taxes.",
    "The shipping line's tax class follows the cart: order 145 holds only reduced-rate items, so its shipping tax is 9%.",
    "The store formats prices with a decimal comma (woocommerce_price_decimal_sep \",\"), but REST prices and totals are always strings with a decimal point.",
    "A review's verified flag is computed by WooCommerce from the reviewer email's purchases; the reviews list answers only approved reviews by default.",
    "Customers' usernames are WooCommerce's, made from the email; passwords were generated by WooCommerce and are not readable. avatar_url values are Gravatar URLs of example.com addresses.",
    "A variation with manage_stock 'parent' reports the parent's stock_quantity.",
    "home_url is wp-env's http://localhost:8888; every email address is at example.com (customers, order billing, reviews, and wp-env's admin wordpress@example.com). system_status.environment.store_id is a random id made at install. Dates are the container's clock at build time."
  ]
}
